Galactic Dan (RISC OS, 1992) - reverse engineering and static recompilation
==========================================================================

A recipe: this repository holds no game data. It rebuilds the game from
your own copy of the disc, recognised by content (recipe.json):

    ./build.sh "Galactic Dan (19xx)(Fourth Dimension).adf"
    cd recomp && ./galdan

The disc can be the TOSEC dump (a cracked copy: its DAN is the game plus
a 96-byte stub) or an unprotected disc made from an original by
tools/mkunprotected.py (its !Runimage is the game). An original disc,
protection and all, isn't enough on its own: its !Runimage is the
protection's encrypted loader, which was run once (tools/run.py, under
tools/arm2.py) to get the game; that isn't automated. build.sh runs
recipe.json's steps with SuperSpider's tools/weave.py (~/stuff/superspider,
or $SUPERSPIDER): it extracts the disc to extracted/disc and !Galactic to
game/ (libroger's appdir), tools/game.py takes the game from it (checked
against its sha256), then make regen and make. Needs python3, OCaml/dune,
gcc and SDL3.

game/                   !Galactic, and GalacticDan_8000,ff8, the decrypted game
                        (absolute, load/exec &8000)
tools/                  the disc and protection tools (adfsd.py: old-map ADFS;
                        mkunprotected.py; run.py) and arm2.py (ARM2 emulator);
                        game.py (above)
ghidra/                 code/data classification and Ghidra import
                          spider.py         recursive-descent + speculative code finder
                          export_ghidra.py  spider -> galdan.json (+ .pickle cache)
                          run_ghidra.sh     headless Ghidra import/analysis/decompile
                          gen_asm.py        galdan.json -> relocatable GNU as source
asm/                    galdan.s: reassembles byte-identically (build.sh) and is
                        relocatable; emu.py / provtrack.py / difftest.py verify it
                        (see asm/README)
recomp/                 static recompilation to C with an SDL3 front end
                        (see recomp/README):
                          python3 gen_c.py --loops && make -j8 && ./galdan
